 to  concentrate safely for any longer than  that they haven't found any mines today  but at least they've made a few more  square metres safe you can't guarantee a  hundred percent safety says Marko 90 or  95 yes but not 100 percent it's not  possible  it's the forestry workers and farmers  who face the remaining risk but I don't  think that's the only reason for the  lack of progress here in the poorer  parts of Eastern Croatia near the forest  where the mine sweepers are working I  meet Sveta Barbic he's an official  representative for the minority rights  of the remaining Serbs still living in  the region most of his relatives didn't  return after the war my uncle built that  old yellow house there he says this one  belongs to my brother this is where my  father was born it all belongs to the  bar [ __ ] family but he's the only  family member still living here  Sveta wants to sell the other properties  but there's a problem it's here  somewhere  the pipe leads into the septic tank he  says but it's been covered over well  under here is the sewage pit her  neighbor built it illegally on my land  but the well is right here he says his  Croatian neighbor didn't care about his  property rights because his a Serbs  Vader says but with the neighbors slurry  pit right next to the well no one wants  to buy the property I've reported it to  the authorities but there was no  reaction that was a few years ago maybe  the time wasn't right  Sveta Babbage points to another Croatian  neighbor with whom he's on friendly  terms he'd like to buy the property but  without the sewage pit under the grass a  neighbor urges fatal Babbage to go to  court over the issue these two at least  get on well money for a case Babbage  says if I go to court I'd need several  thousand euros and it would take a long  time only people with a lot of money can  afford to sue these days  you know what but you never cry legal  costs in Croatia are more expensive than  in Germany court cases last four 